     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Yes that is correct. You should refer to below:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt;margin-left:0in;background:white\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:#24292e\">Tumor phylogeny analysis by WES</span></b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:#24292e\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:#24292e;background:white\">\r\n<i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">Experimental design</span></i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">: WES/WGS of multiple spatially or temporally separated tumor samples with matched normal, greater than 20 normal controls (no need\r\n to be matched)<u></u><u></u></span></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:#24292e;margin-top:3.0pt;background:white\">\r\n<i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">Script</span></i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">: <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/somatic_SNV.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/somatic_SNV.sh&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UiOMDcW6GA3rC_0bs0Dct\"><span style=\"color:#0366d6\">Profiling somatic point mutations</span></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3icRfa1OF5alYf0YUrbHtr\"><span style=\"color:#0366d6\">CODEX2\r\n --&gt; FALCON-X</span></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/Canopy.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/Canopy.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JyxIsvEX0tWuuGf-fsSKH\"><span style=\"color:#0366d6\">Canopy</span></a><u></u><u></u></span></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:#24292e;margin-top:3.0pt;background:white\">\r\n<i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">More details</span></i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">: <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1wboQZs5zk6tZTGdQjLWFP\"><span style=\"color:#0366d6\">CODEX2</span></a>, <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/package=falconx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/package%3Dfalconx&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZsdKFYhwZ0l_VTuncNBoQ\"><span style=\"color:#0366d6\">FALCON-X</span></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nfH1mczA_obqm8nrimpYL\"><span style=\"color:#0366d6\">Canopy</span></a><u></u><u></u></span></li></ul>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> Patidar, Rajesh (NIH/NCI) [C] [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rajesh....@nih.gov</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, November 8, 2017 9:51 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Jiang, Yuchao &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@email.unc.edu</a>&gt;; Hao Chen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hxc...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> RE: falconx<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Hi Yuchao,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Thanks for the email. Could you please let me know if my following understanding is correct or not?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Steps:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Run\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1y_8xv7kCmziK-HGbRk2t9\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2.R</a> ==&gt; I ran this successfully\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Run\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3icRfa1OF5alYf0YUrbHtr\">\r\nhttps://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R</a> <u></u>\r\n<u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Run\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/Canopy.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/Canopy.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441753000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JyxIsvEX0tWuuGf-fsSKH\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/Canopy.R</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Where does a test sample fit in this procedure? Sorry but for different scripts different example data is used which is making me a bit confusing as I am not an R expert yet.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Rajesh<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> Jiang, Yuchao [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mailto:yuc...@email.unc.edu</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, November 8, 2017 9:33 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Patidar, Rajesh (NIH/NCI) [C] &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rajesh....@nih.gov</a>&gt;; Hao Chen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hxc...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> RE: falconx<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Hi Rajesh,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">We tried as much as we can to give a unified framework/script. However, a lot of the upstream processing are different across different research groups – this\r\n includes different data quality (and thus different QC should be adopted) and even different vcf format (depending on which caller you need). With this said, we also recommend that you run the demo code with the demo dataset yourself first before applying\r\n CODEX2/FALCON-X/Canopy to your dataset. The change from the demo to your dataset should not be on the major functions of these software but mostly, if not all, on the pre-processing step and post-calling quality control/filtering.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Hope this helps! If we have more bandwidth to further integrate the codes, we will let you know.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Yuchao<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> Patidar, Rajesh (NIH/NCI) [C] [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mailto:rajesh....@nih.gov</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, November 8, 2017 7:45 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Hao Chen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hxc...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b> Jiang, Yuchao &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@email.unc.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: falconx<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thanks Hao, I think MARATHON explains it in much better way. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I noticed that most of the scripts are based on some published datasets and I have to edit a lot to make them work on patients(PDX) where I usually have 4-6 time\r\n points or more. Is there a script which can take multiple bams  and vcfs from a patient and can run the whole pipeline (CODEX2 ==&gt;Canopy)?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Rajesh<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">From:\r\n</span></b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hao Chen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hxc...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Tuesday, November 7, 2017 at 5:00 PM<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>&quot;Patidar, Rajesh (NIH/NCI) [C]&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rajesh....@nih.gov</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc: </b>&quot;Jiang, Yuchao&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@email.unc.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Re: falconx<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hi Rajesh,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">This website documents the analysis from BAM file to canopy: <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498441754000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2J5GVVx4INzaYf-nKwz83T\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON</a> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">You can find example codes there.  From BAM files, you would first need to use CODEX to generate inputs for falconx (Figure 1 on that webpage gives an overview\r\n of the process).  I am also cc&#39;ing Yuchao, the developer of CODEX and Canopy in case you have questions there.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Best,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hao<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">On Tue, Nov 7, 2017 at 10:45 AM, Patidar, Rajesh (NIH/NCI) [C] &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rajesh....@nih.gov</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hi Hao,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Could you please share how do I run falconx on a bam file? How do I create the baseline first I think\r\n would be first question and then how to use the tumor bam file to run falconx to create input for the canopy package.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Rajesh<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
